  "id": "system",
  "term": "system",
  "definition": "In this context, a moral orienting system is the relatively steady pattern through which a person’s values, beliefs, actions, relationships, and experiences work together to shape how they see the world and make choices. If this system cannot absorb moral stress, the person may become morally disoriented.",
